      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=60785ded115da6006f540529",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Somewhat related to this conversation, there are currently three authorization modules:</p>\n<ul class=\"alternate\" type=\"square\">\n\t<li>webac - <a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo-module-auth-webac\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo-module-auth-webac</a></li>\n\t<li>rbacl - <a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo-module-auth-rbacl\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo-module-auth-rbacl</a></li>\n\t<li>xacml - <a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo-module-auth-xacml\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo-module-auth-xacml</a></li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<p>Given that the fcrepo-specification only includes mention of webac, we should be planning on deprecating rbacl and xacml... and therefore consolidating/refactoring webac, auth-common, and parts of rbacl that webac depends upon.</p>",
     "created": "09/Feb/17 10:16 AM",
     "id": "18548",
     "jsdPublic": true,
